# Shell scripts must be LF, whatever they are for: a CRLF script piped to `sh`
# fails on its first line, and nothing in the toolchain warns first.
#
# UNANCHORED on purpose. A pattern containing a slash anywhere but at the end is
# anchored to this file's directory, so `scripts/*.sh` would silently stop
# matching the day a script moved.
*.sh text eol=lf
